---
// Knock's Postgres 11.9 -> 15.3 upgrade by logical replication, before and at cutover.
// Source: Knock, "Zero downtime Postgres upgrades". Plain inline SVG with site tokens.
function arrow(x1: number, y1: number, x2: number, y2: number) {
  const a = Math.atan2(y2 - y1, x2 - x1);
  const len = 9;
  const bx = x2 - len * Math.cos(a), by = y2 - len * Math.sin(a);
  const head = `${x2},${y2} ${bx + 4.5 * Math.sin(a)},${by - 4.5 * Math.cos(a)} ${bx - 4.5 * Math.sin(a)},${by + 4.5 * Math.cos(a)}`;
  return { line: { x1, y1, x2: bx, y2: by }, head };
}
const W = 900, H = 380;
const app = { x: 340, y: 20, w: 220, h: 56 };
const oldDb = { x: 20, y: 180, w: 250, h: 80 };
const newDb = { x: 630, y: 180, w: 250, h: 80 };
const appOld = arrow(app.x, 60, oldDb.x + oldDb.w / 2, oldDb.y);
const appNew = arrow(app.x + app.w, 60, newDb.x + newDb.w / 2, newDb.y);
const rep = arrow(oldDb.x + oldDb.w, 220, newDb.x, 220);
---
<figure class="rf">
  <div class="rf-scroll">
  <svg viewBox={`0 0 ${W} ${H}`} role="img" aria-label="Knock's upgrade. The application first talks to the old Postgres 11.9 primary. Logical replication through a publication and subscription copies tables, one at a time, to a new Postgres 15.3 server. Sequences are not copied, so each one is set ahead by 100,000 before cutover. At cutover the app sends new queries to the new server and gives running queries 500 milliseconds to finish.">
    <rect x={app.x} y={app.y} width={app.w} height={app.h} rx="4" class="box" />
    <text x="450" y="46" text-anchor="middle" class="t-h"><tspan data-lang-en>Application</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>Ứng dụng</tspan></text>

    <line {...appOld.line} class="edge" /><polygon points={appOld.head} class="head" />
    <text x="20" y="100" text-anchor="start" class="t-note"><tspan data-lang-en>before: all queries</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>trước: mọi query</tspan></text>
    <line {...appNew.line} class="edge dash" /><polygon points={appNew.head} class="head" />
    <text x="700" y="100" text-anchor="start" class="t-note"><tspan data-lang-en>at cutover: new queries</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>lúc chuyển: query mới</tspan></text>
    <text x="20" y="118" text-anchor="start" class="t-note"><tspan data-lang-en>running ones get 500 ms</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>query đang chạy có 500 ms</tspan></text>

    <rect x={oldDb.x} y={oldDb.y} width={oldDb.w} height={oldDb.h} rx="4" class="box strong" />
    <text x="145" y="214" text-anchor="middle" class="t-h">Postgres 11.9</text>
    <text x="145" y="236" text-anchor="middle" class="t-note"><tspan data-lang-en>old primary, publication</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>primary cũ, publication</tspan></text>
    <rect x={newDb.x} y={newDb.y} width={newDb.w} height={newDb.h} rx="4" class="box strong" />
    <text x="755" y="214" text-anchor="middle" class="t-h">Postgres 15.3</text>
    <text x="755" y="236" text-anchor="middle" class="t-note"><tspan data-lang-en>new server, subscription</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>server mới, subscription</tspan></text>

    <line {...rep.line} class="edge" /><polygon points={rep.head} class="head" />
    <text x="450" y="206" text-anchor="middle" class="t-h"><tspan data-lang-en>logical replication</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>logical replication</tspan></text>
    <text x="450" y="244" text-anchor="middle" class="t-note"><tspan data-lang-en>row changes, one table at a time</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>thay đổi theo hàng, từng bảng một</tspan></text>

    <rect x="20" y="300" width="860" height="56" rx="4" class="box bad" />
    <text x="40" y="324" class="t-bad"><tspan data-lang-en>Not replicated: sequences (ID counters)</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>Không được replicate: sequence (bộ đếm ID)</tspan></text>
    <text x="40" y="344" class="t-note"><tspan data-lang-en>Before cutover, set each one on the new server to the old next value plus 100,000.</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>Trước khi chuyển, đặt mỗi sequence ở server mới bằng giá trị kế tiếp của server cũ cộng 100.000.</tspan></text>
  </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption>
    <span data-lang-en>Simplified from Knock's post. The upgrade works because the log describes rows, not disk blocks, so two Postgres versions can talk to each other.</span>
    <span data-lang-vi>Giản lược từ bài của Knock. Cách này chạy được vì log mô tả hàng dữ liệu chứ không phải khối đĩa, nên hai phiên bản Postgres nói chuyện được với nhau.</span>
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .rf { margin: 2em 0; width: 100%; }
  .rf-scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
  .rf svg { display: block; width: 100%; min-width: 640px; height: auto; }
  .rf text { font-size: 14px; fill: var(--text-body); }
  .rf .t-h { font-size: 15px; font-weight: 700; fill: var(--text); }
  .rf .t-note { font-size: 12.5px; fill: var(--text-muted); }
  .rf .t-bad { fill: var(--red); font-weight: 700; font-size: 13px; }
  .rf .t-ok { fill: var(--text); font-weight: 700; font-size: 13px; }
  .rf .box { fill: var(--bg-alt); stroke: var(--text-muted); stroke-width: 1.2; }
  .rf .box.strong { stroke: var(--text); stroke-width: 1.8; }
  .rf .box.bad { stroke: var(--red); stroke-width: 1.8; }
  .rf .edge { stroke: var(--text-muted); stroke-width: 1.4; fill: none; }
  .rf .edge.dash { stroke-dasharray: 5 4; }
  .rf .edge.bad { stroke: var(--red); stroke-dasharray: 5 4; }
  .rf .head { fill: var(--text-muted); }
  .rf .head.bad { fill: var(--red); }
  .rf figcaption { margin-top: 10px; font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.55; text-align: center; }
</style>
